    "thumbnail": "2d3a0a0fbc43"
  },
  "lines": {
    "p001": {
      "source_hash": "359dcc989d68",
      "text": "Chief! At noon, on the roof,"
    },
    "p002": {
      "source_hash": "93903113d3c2",
      "text": "and the sky was so blue!"
    },
    "p003": {
      "source_hash": "399fe677e849",
      "text": "But I went back at dusk,"
    },
    "p004": {
      "source_hash": "f422e39aefdb",
      "text": "and the sun was a big red ball!"
    },
    "p005": {
      "source_hash": "2588d80d4900",
      "text": "Same sun, and the same sunlight."
    },
    "p006": {
      "source_hash": "c460be6aca94",
      "text": "You see it every day. So who changed its color?"
    },
    "p007": {
      "source_hash": "c40e35ee1293",
      "text": "Someone swapped colors!"
    },
    "p008": {
      "source_hash": "6bb012daf243",
      "text": "Something's up to tricks. It's right by you, but you can't see it."
    },
    "p009": {
      "source_hash": "4c5e7994f937",
      "text": "So the sky's blue,"
    },
    "p010": {
      "source_hash": "e438a3a039f5",
      "text": "where's it come from?"
    },
    "p011": {
      "source_hash": "667197ef2057",
      "text": "First, a guess: water, a few drops of milk, a flashlight,"
    },
    "p012": {
      "source_hash": "5e158249342f",
      "text": "from the side, what color is it?"
    },
    "p013": {
      "source_hash": "a280f0cc0dac",
      "text": "Water with milk?"
    },
    "p014": {
      "source_hash": "8192526ab386",
      "text": "Kind of white?"
    },
    "p015": {
      "source_hash": "ef1344210186",
      "text": "And on the Moon, by day, look up:"
    },
    "p016": {
      "source_hash": "3a05296e14e4",
      "text": "what color is the sky?"
    },
    "p017": {
      "source_hash": "c5d998c9f208",
      "text": "The Moon? No idea."
    },
    "p018": {
      "source_hash": "a2c0ad3b631b",
      "text": "And there are clouds!"
    },
    "p019": {
      "source_hash": "0507d20deeec",
      "text": "If the sky's blue, why are clouds white?"
    },
    "p020": {
      "source_hash": "c52f77a460df",
      "text": "Same sun,"
    },
    "p021": {
      "source_hash": "aeaff2e9259a",
      "text": "so why blue, then red?"
    },
    "p022": {
      "source_hash": "1c5086ac1e1e",
      "text": "Isn't the sky just blue?"
    },
    "p023": {
      "source_hash": "a433325e939a",
      "text": "If it were just blue,"
    },
    "p024": {
      "source_hash": "b1632b6b567d",
      "text": "why does it go black after sunset?"
    },
    "p025": {
      "source_hash": "980e8c0e98a0",
      "text": "Because... the sun went home?"
    },
    "p026": {
      "source_hash": "158431070b07",
      "text": "Yes. Sun gone, blue gone."
    },
    "p027": {
      "source_hash": "b1adeffda7c6",
      "text": "So that blue comes from sunlight."
    },
    "p028": {
      "source_hash": "a67375b88157",
      "text": "But sunlight is white,"
    },
    "p029": {
      "source_hash": "34349b2e58b1",
      "text": "Where's blue?"
    },
    "p030": {
      "source_hash": "9aee72e854a7",
      "text": "White light is many colors mixed."
    },
    "p031": {
      "source_hash": "20b1c6614d12",
      "text": "They hit your eyes together; you see white."
    },
    "p032": {
      "source_hash": "cc1f2d274a66",
      "text": "Watering plants, you may see a tiny rainbow in the spray."
    },
    "p033": {
      "source_hash": "35de29603d90",
      "text": "Those colors were hiding in sunlight."
    },
    "p034": {
      "source_hash": "d67462368831",
      "text": "Point a glass prism at the sun,"
    },
    "p035": {
      "source_hash": "29d14a50e868",
      "text": "and a row of colors shows on the wall."
    },
    "p036": {
      "source_hash": "3e66aee63d3b",
      "text": "Long ago, the English scientist Newton split sunlight with a prism."
    },
    "p037": {
      "source_hash": "f20aa8c149e6",
      "text": "Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet!"
    },
    "p038": {
      "source_hash": "a8c680ab58bb",
      "text": "All squeezed into white light?"
    },
    "p039": {
      "source_hash": "5de5b9ccf96e",
      "text": "Yes, every one."
    },
    "p040": {
      "source_hash": "5385ef130b9b",
      "text": "White light is crowded!"
    },
    "p041": {
      "source_hash": "1dc2c3d5a291",
      "text": "So colors,"
    },
    "p042": {
      "source_hash": "6305cadc906a",
      "text": "how are they different?"
    },
    "p043": {
      "source_hash": "c792faecfffc",
      "text": "Ever swung a jump rope? It makes waves."
    },
    "p044": {
      "source_hash": "01d174a85182",
      "text": "Light travels like that, wave after wave."
    },
    "p045": {
      "source_hash": "769969e838e4",
      "text": "Red has long waves, like big slow swings;"
    },
    "p046": {
      "source_hash": "cf969f73f282",
      "text": "blue and violet have short ones, like quick shakes."
    },
    "p047": {
      "source_hash": "cca756e1d1c0",
      "text": "Wave top to wave top: that's wavelength."
    },
    "p048": {
      "source_hash": "37865381b807",
      "text": "Different wavelengths, different colors."
    },
    "p049": {
      "source_hash": "96e7dd27d797",
      "text": "Faster, shorter waves!"
    },
    "p050": {
      "source_hash": "c1f9ddf1b223",
      "text": "So blue is a shorter wave?"
    },
    "p051": {
      "source_hash": "d6fc6a4d5916",
      "text": "Yes. Remember that. It'll be back."
    },
    "p052": {
      "source_hash": "07340dbe30d4",
      "text": "So is the sky blue"
    },
    "p053": {
      "source_hash": "1a2dec7eb0fc",
      "text": "because air is blue?"
    },
    "p054": {
      "source_hash": "39fb18fff83a",
      "text": "Take an empty jar, full of air."
    },
    "p055": {
      "source_hash": "f1d6d4578412",
      "text": "See any blue?"
    },
    "p056": {
      "source_hash": "9736f68480b4",
      "text": "I can't."
    },
    "p057": {
      "source_hash": "4bf8d74b0f68",
      "text": "It's clear."
    },
    "p058": {
      "source_hash": "28bfe66a3e65",
      "text": "A jar of air: no color."
    },
    "p059": {
      "source_hash": "f65a22afe062",
      "text": "But the air above your head is a very, very thick layer."
    },
    "p060": {
      "source_hash": "d6e7748d70ea",
      "text": "From high up it's clear: US Air Force photos at 20 km"
    },
    "p061": {
      "source_hash": "83b2aa86cba9",
      "text": "and Earth's edge is a thin blue ring."
    },
    "p062": {
      "source_hash": "3debe8696307",
      "text": "That air is made of tiny, tiny molecules."
    },
    "p063": {
      "source_hash": "40d0bd86afb8",
      "text": "Molecules? What are those?"
    },
    "p064": {
      "source_hash": "55f78335fd4e",
      "text": "Think of tiny balls in the air,"
    },
    "p065": {
      "source_hash": "3587fa4a9fcb",
      "text": "too small to see."
    },
    "p066": {
      "source_hash": "d223bfdc678f",
      "text": "I breathe in little balls too?"
    },
    "p067": {
      "source_hash": "f72ee31c72ae",
      "text": "Yes. Every breath, you take in a huge number."
    },
    "p068": {
      "source_hash": "fe5196ab94e3",
      "text": "A molecule is about 1,000 times smaller than a light wave."
    },
    "p069": {
      "source_hash": "f3ebe7dd8e38",
      "text": "1,000?"
    },
    "p070": {
      "source_hash": "39e0ac976cbe",
      "text": "Then light just goes through?"
    },
    "p071": {
      "source_hash": "2da2072169da",
      "text": "Mostly, yes."
    },
    "p072": {
      "source_hash": "de6a74a94fcc",
      "text": "But some light hits them and bounces off,"
    },
    "p073": {
      "source_hash": "3e36511f1a75",
      "text": "all ways: scattering."
    },
    "p074": {
      "source_hash": "00f9c47d0fe2",
      "text": "The bounced light hits other balls and bounces again."
    },
    "p075": {
      "source_hash": "f483723e9c37",
      "text": "Like marbles!"
    },
    "p076": {
      "source_hash": "b1763f23689e",
      "text": "A bit, but it bounces in every direction."
    },
    "p077": {
      "source_hash": "dc662e6d4567",
      "text": "Each one"
    },
    "p078": {
      "source_hash": "6f3510a04842",
      "text": "gets bounced?"
    },
    "p079": {
      "source_hash": "272f6fc1edc9",
      "text": "Yes. But remember those short little waves?"
    },
    "p080": {
      "source_hash": "e86a4e375852",
      "text": "They get bounced the most."
    },
    "p081": {
      "source_hash": "de5606fb786f",
      "text": "Blue gets bounced several times more than red."
    },
    "p082": {
      "source_hash": "6f293f74f385",
      "text": "Several times? Busy blue!"
    },
    "p083": {
      "source_hash": "8c3f2d5b0f70",
      "text": "And red?"
    },
    "p084": {
      "source_hash": "48d738a1182e",
      "text": "Red bounces aside less."
    },
    "p085": {
      "source_hash": "75b4bbcc434d",
      "text": "It mostly goes straight ahead."
    },
    "p086": {
      "source_hash": "e356deacc5e2",
      "text": "Red is so focused!"
    },
    "p087": {
      "source_hash": "c919df334551",
      "text": "In the 1800s, Englishman Rayleigh did the math."
    },
    "p088": {
      "source_hash": "d68bc88eb47b",
      "text": "So this is called Rayleigh scattering."
    },
    "p089": {
      "source_hash": "ccec91a85569",
      "text": "Funny: back then, they thought"
    },
    "p090": {
      "source_hash": "f4ea1ff5fb19",
      "text": "dust and tiny water drops bounced the blue."
    },
    "p091": {
      "source_hash": "8404530f6ba4",
      "text": "Later, scientists saw: with dust,"
    },
    "p092": {
      "source_hash": "bd2b0d306bfe",
      "text": "the blue would vary by weather,"
    },
    "p093": {
      "source_hash": "d6d68f6bb66f",
      "text": "but it really doesn't."
    },
    "p094": {
      "source_hash": "c8b27c10949e",
      "text": "Then, in 1910, physicist Einstein calculated"
    },
    "p095": {
      "source_hash": "885313c7f4eb",
      "text": "air molecules alone turn the sky blue."
    },
    "p096": {
      "source_hash": "b482a5344430",
      "text": "Einstein too"
    },
    "p097": {
      "source_hash": "0a18c4918660",
      "text": "did sky math!"
    },
    "p098": {
      "source_hash": "22690e648c02",
      "text": "So anywhere you look up,"
    },
    "p099": {
      "source_hash": "de3eceb6963a",
      "text": "bounced blue light is reaching your eyes."
    },
    "p100": {
      "source_hash": "1067b470b681",
      "text": "Not blue;"
    },
    "p101": {
      "source_hash": "7a6482c5624e",
      "text": "It keeps bouncing blue light to you."
    },
    "p102": {
      "source_hash": "a47640d9638f",
      "text": "So the color thief"
    },
    "p103": {
      "source_hash": "87a77138a0f0",
      "text": "was the air!"
    },
    "p104": {
      "source_hash": "db3693e8e436",
      "text": "But I heard"
    },
    "p105": {
      "source_hash": "92278e65d14b",
      "text": "the sky reflects the sea."
    },
    "p106": {
      "source_hash": "10b0c536b9fc",
      "text": "Many do."
    },
    "p107": {
      "source_hash": "4a663be28048",
      "text": "But on a mountain far, far from the sea, the sky's still blue."
    },
    "p108": {
      "source_hash": "796a2eb5fa61",
      "text": "Often it's reversed: on a beach,"
    },
    "p109": {
      "source_hash": "5af502f85d60",
      "text": "the sea looks blue partly by mirroring sky."
    },
    "p110": {
      "source_hash": "534eed7b8bb0",
      "text": "Wait, violet waves are shorter,"
    },
    "p111": {
      "source_hash": "42fbb03c2924",
      "text": "so why isn't the sky violet?"
    },
    "p112": {
      "source_hash": "01d2f49f95cf",
      "text": "Good one. Sunlight has less violet to start."
    },
    "p113": {
      "source_hash": "d72db7f19f36",
      "text": "Some gets absorbed by air very high up."
    },
    "p114": {
      "source_hash": "049bd393b768",
      "text": "Swallowed: it never reaches the ground."
    },
    "p115": {
      "source_hash": "b3e1599ecf98",
      "text": "The air sneaks a snack!"
    },
    "p116": {
      "source_hash": "76e55647b584",
      "text": "And our eyes are less sensitive to violet."
    },
    "p117": {
      "source_hash": "2973e626ccdc",
      "text": "There's violet up there, mixed in,"
    },
    "p118": {
      "source_hash": "9cfdf825de3c",
      "text": "so to us it looks pale blue."
    },
    "p119": {
      "source_hash": "66a1dacd43cc",
      "text": "My eye"
    },
    "p120": {
      "source_hash": "e1fcf87d15eb",
      "text": "pick colors too?"
    },
    "p121": {
      "source_hash": "9bce10fd5342",
      "text": "That's the fun part:"
    },
    "p122": {
      "source_hash": "a67f42ee92d4",
      "text": "your eyes help pick the color."
    },
    "p123": {
      "source_hash": "85839d2a19ad",
      "text": "My eyes are a palette!"
    },
    "p124": {
      "source_hash": "a9cd9b4e876e",
      "text": "Lots of blue bounces off,"
    },
    "p125": {
      "source_hash": "3d690fc04bcc",
      "text": "so what color is the sun itself?"
    },
    "p126": {
      "source_hash": "a9763055424e",
      "text": "I"
    },
    "p127": {
      "source_hash": "3974109d62f3",
      "text": "use yellow."
    },
    "p128": {
      "source_hash": "d74f155f0cb4",
      "text": "Lots of people do. But to see the sun itself, leave the ground."
    },
    "p129": {
      "source_hash": "64573df225d4",
      "text": "From space, it's white."
    },
    "p130": {
      "source_hash": "a5d102f98438",
      "text": "Up there, you're above most of the air."
    },
    "p131": {
      "source_hash": "50ecc6ebff1d",
      "text": "Here it looks yellow"
    },
    "p132": {
      "source_hash": "25bb727d99c5",
      "text": "because some blue got bounced away on the way."
    },
    "p133": {
      "source_hash": "9d65d752aed5",
      "text": "With less blue,"
    },
    "p134": {
      "source_hash": "4a86c923c0aa",
      "text": "why's the sun so bright?"
    },
    "p135": {
      "source_hash": "5e0418faf7a3",
      "text": "Not much is lost."
    },
    "p136": {
      "source_hash": "cbf984c59dd4",
      "text": "On clear days, over half the sunlight still reaches us."
    },
    "p137": {
      "source_hash": "e6fba31ac6aa",
      "text": "No wonder"
    },
    "p138": {
      "source_hash": "81ad0a9226d1",
      "text": "days are still bright!"
    },
    "p139": {
      "source_hash": "3f8d8cf04f0a",
      "text": "So at sunset, is the sun"
    },
    "p140": {
      "source_hash": "2f5373350ab7",
      "text": "burning hotter?"
    },
    "p141": {
      "source_hash": "37904b26bfe2",
      "text": "The sun's the same at noon and dusk. Not it."
    },
    "p142": {
      "source_hash": "fff02cb31264",
      "text": "What changes is the light's path to you."
    },
    "p143": {
      "source_hash": "184faf155632",
      "text": "The path changes?"
    },
    "p144": {
      "source_hash": "95799511bd9a",
      "text": "The sun isn't farther."
    },
    "p145": {
      "source_hash": "6a24c055fbf3",
      "text": "Same distance"
    },
    "p146": {
      "source_hash": "a07d954ca271",
      "text": "What changes is the air the light must cross: much thicker."
    },
    "p147": {
      "source_hash": "c3d0f1a1eb7f",
      "text": "Sun overhead:"
    },
    "p148": {
      "source_hash": "53b51b509166",
      "text": "light comes straight down: less air."
    },
    "p149": {
      "source_hash": "af7cd98c3cf6",
      "text": "Near sunset, light slants in,"
    },
    "p150": {
      "source_hash": "041f1151e600",
      "text": "skimming the ground."
    },
    "p151": {
      "source_hash": "3cca765a0d37",
      "text": "Sun on the horizon, the air light crosses"
    },
    "p152": {
      "source_hash": "9c524ce14986",
      "text": "is about 30-some times the overhead."
    },
    "p153": {
      "source_hash": "f2ffe8814fe2",
      "text": "30-some?"
    },
    "p154": {
      "source_hash": "ab1e7b5e3427",
      "text": "Thick!"
    },
    "p155": {
      "source_hash": "93ae7eca92e6",
      "text": "Light's long trip!"
    },
    "p156": {
      "source_hash": "1da4347dfd22",
      "text": "On that long trip, blue bounces off, off, and off."
    },
    "p157": {
      "source_hash": "297d3a3a20e6",
      "text": "By the time it reaches you, it's mostly red, orange."
    },
    "p158": {
      "source_hash": "900ba4f0f891",
      "text": "So the lower the sun, usually the redder."
    },
    "p159": {
      "source_hash": "cacd1fb532f7",
      "text": "But even a red sun: don't stare at it. It can hurt your eyes."
    },
    "p160": {
      "source_hash": "14a10be94a7c",
      "text": "And sunrise,"
    },
    "p161": {
      "source_hash": "3276b56fc9df",
      "text": "Same thing?"
    },
    "p162": {
      "source_hash": "a6c99c81082d",
      "text": "Yes. At sunrise light also skims in at a slant,"
    },
    "p163": {
      "source_hash": "a51dbc3bdf92",
      "text": "just from the east."
    },
    "p164": {
      "source_hash": "34c948294e43",
      "text": "The blue bounced away,"
    },
    "p165": {
      "source_hash": "5e7da7bedc4d",
      "text": "where does it go?"
    },
    "p166": {
      "source_hash": "ba356b11452b",
      "text": "Into other skies."
    },
    "p167": {
      "source_hash": "cd29b3d0192c",
      "text": "While you're watching a red sun,"
    },
    "p168": {
      "source_hash": "5707c62a2095",
      "text": "blue from that light"
    },
    "p169": {
      "source_hash": "bdf381a41b9c",
      "text": "gives far places an afternoon blue sky."
    },
    "p170": {
      "source_hash": "5b4ee32e76aa",
      "text": "US weather scientist Corfidi said:"
    },
    "p171": {
      "source_hash": "d30e7c473200",
      "text": "sunsets are red because day skies are blue."
    },
    "p172": {
      "source_hash": "e48a2cb6e138",
      "text": "The sunset I see"
    },
    "p173": {
      "source_hash": "e325bd82795a",
      "text": "is someone's blue sky!"
    },
    "p174": {
      "source_hash": "9b089e737afd",
      "text": "Now for the water with milk."
    },
    "p175": {
      "source_hash": "f4c0fb031bf8",
      "text": "Light from the side; look from there:"
    },
    "p176": {
      "source_hash": "2ae7817807ee",
      "text": "the water has a faint blue tint."
    },
    "p177": {
      "source_hash": "8b18b42df368",
      "text": "Facing the light,"
    },
    "p178": {
      "source_hash": "5b0c9a5a071c",
      "text": "the light coming through looks orange and red."
    },
    "p179": {
      "source_hash": "0d8c010f37b8",
      "text": "A cup:"
    },
    "p180": {
      "source_hash": "a71250a807b3",
      "text": "sky and sunset!"
    },
    "p181": {
      "source_hash": "a488a925f5e5",
      "text": "What's the milk doing?"
    },
    "p182": {
      "source_hash": "f1011bb37e67",
      "text": "Milk's tiny bits bounce light, like air."
    },
    "p183": {
      "source_hash": "0e4c7c555e8b",
      "text": "The farther light goes, the more blue is lost."
    },
    "p184": {
      "source_hash": "04235f8407e3",
      "text": "Try it: water, a few drops of milk, a flashlight."
    },
    "p185": {
      "source_hash": "cb60fb907f7f",
      "text": "No color? Add two more drops."
    },
    "p186": {
      "source_hash": "202f90caa7ee",
      "text": "I'll borrow Dad's!"
    },
    "p187": {
      "source_hash": "331f7b8203d6",
      "text": "Then look out at the clouds."
    },
    "p188": {
      "source_hash": "fadc654fc221",
      "text": "Same sun on clouds,"
    },
    "p189": {
      "source_hash": "42717f4c62ce",
      "text": "so why aren't they blue or red?"
    },
    "p190": {
      "source_hash": "bdca4fe24f6a",
      "text": "Clouds are water drops,"
    },
    "p191": {
      "source_hash": "209ea7dc2a83",
      "text": "and a water drop is much bigger than an air molecule."
    },
    "p192": {
      "source_hash": "2de7489656cb",
      "text": "Big drops bounce all colors alike."
    },
    "p193": {
      "source_hash": "e9b032c58c60",
      "text": "All the colors bouncing together mix into white."
    },
    "p194": {
      "source_hash": "3ea4c9a87eb2",
      "text": "Fog too"
    },
    "p195": {
      "source_hash": "87ab3fca9638",
      "text": "are white too!"
    },
    "p196": {
      "source_hash": "0d8705337bb9",
      "text": "Yes, fog is drops too."
    },
    "p197": {
      "source_hash": "28cc1291880d",
      "text": "When the sun hits morning fog, it's all white."
    },
    "p198": {
      "source_hash": "096cf100ff60",
      "text": "And before rain,"
    },
    "p199": {
      "source_hash": "a49ca342221f",
      "text": "why do clouds turn gray?"
    },
    "p200": {
      "source_hash": "debd39058546",
      "text": "Thick clouds block much light,"
    },
    "p201": {
      "source_hash": "f4c4c4f11a4c",
      "text": "so less light below: they look gray, dark."
    },
    "p202": {
      "source_hash": "a09fa90612ab",
      "text": "Sometimes it's the bright sky beside it"
    },
    "p203": {
      "source_hash": "854eb314ec0d",
      "text": "next to it, your eyes see gray."
    },
    "p204": {
      "source_hash": "b99766fe85ca",
      "text": "Eyes picking colors again!"
    },
    "p205": {
      "source_hash": "88f8aebe71a3",
      "text": "But clouds at sunset"
    },
    "p206": {
      "source_hash": "149c59706ff3",
      "text": "are orange and pink!"
    },
    "p207": {
      "source_hash": "f167840b08db",
      "text": "Their light was already bounced red."
    },
    "p208": {
      "source_hash": "76dda1609829",
      "text": "A cloud's a big screen, bouncing color to you."
    },
    "p209": {
      "source_hash": "78e9be674495",
      "text": "The sky's a movie!"
    },
    "p210": {
      "source_hash": "ad76bbb00ac6",
      "text": "Water drops change sky colors, and so does dust."
    },
    "p211": {
      "source_hash": "18eb01506344",
      "text": "So more dust"
    },
    "p212": {
      "source_hash": "39aeaed5ad50",
      "text": "means bluer sky?"
    },
    "p213": {
      "source_hash": "c0f53b37b4e3",
      "text": "Remember the old guess?"
    },
    "p214": {
      "source_hash": "e179d912c45d",
      "text": "You think like them, but the answer is the opposite."
    },
    "p215": {
      "source_hash": "ab61cb8a3ab8",
      "text": "Dust and smoke,"
    },
    "p216": {
      "source_hash": "b1c5f1096b01",
      "text": "so the day's blue fades, like a white veil."
    },
    "p217": {
      "source_hash": "0406544ca89a",
      "text": "That's called haze."
    },
    "p218": {
      "source_hash": "c6965cc45d0f",
      "text": "With lots of haze, even noon sky looks white."
    },
    "p219": {
      "source_hash": "d796cdaee5e0",
      "text": "So the bluest days"
    },
    "p220": {
      "source_hash": "2f913d9d8aef",
      "text": "often have clean air."
    },
    "p221": {
      "source_hash": "395741146707",
      "text": "No wonder some days the sky is extra blue!"
    },
    "p222": {
      "source_hash": "010f31caab6b",
      "text": "Lots of dust,"
    },
    "p223": {
      "source_hash": "6d63d07ef812",
      "text": "what about sunsets?"
    },
    "p224": {
      "source_hash": "745fb293b0f4",
      "text": "Hard to say: sometimes redder,"
    },
    "p225": {
      "source_hash": "a9222d32492f",
      "text": "sometimes just gray and hazy."
    },
    "p226": {
      "source_hash": "581d68aa9503",
      "text": "Fly on a hazy evening: the sunset below looks pale;"
    },
    "p227": {
      "source_hash": "d7de34c5bc13",
      "text": "once the plane climbs above the haze, colors pop."
    },
    "p228": {
      "source_hash": "73c202ab3394",
      "text": "The haze hid the colors!"
    },
    "p229": {
      "source_hash": "a4d1898bcf93",
      "text": "Haze stays low, so high clouds glow reddest:"
    },
    "p230": {
      "source_hash": "03d0933e1ad7",
      "text": "their light skipped the haze."
    },
    "p231": {
      "source_hash": "865835294385",
      "text": "High clouds glow reddest!"
    },
    "p232": {
      "source_hash": "f8776d5d2f46",
      "text": "An even stranger glow came from a volcano."
    },
    "p233": {
      "source_hash": "e334a7a3fd9d",
      "text": "In 1991, Mount Pinatubo in the Philippines erupted."
    },
    "p234": {
      "source_hash": "a8ab2f84aab4",
      "text": "Its gas turned into fine droplets high in the sky,"
    },
    "p235": {
      "source_hash": "b86f6b8d020a",
      "text": "spreading out about 20 to 30 km up."
    },
    "p236": {
      "source_hash": "d5f1b0bc253c",
      "text": "So high?"
    },
    "p237": {
      "source_hash": "c72b7d68f826",
      "text": "Seen from the ground?"
    },
    "p238": {
      "source_hash": "420b70b89c51",
      "text": "15 minutes after sunset,"
    },
    "p239": {
      "source_hash": "4044f0094e16",
      "text": "but that high layer still caught sunlight, glowing lilac and orange-red."
    },
    "p240": {
      "source_hash": "944895994a1a",
      "text": "These glows lingered about 18 months."
    },
    "p241": {
      "source_hash": "7a41c7d038a2",
      "text": "Even in the US, across the world, people saw them."
    },
    "p242": {
      "source_hash": "52ec278e3e90",
      "text": "A volcano"
    },
    "p243": {
      "source_hash": "2925a0c7ad27",
      "text": "change color!"
    },
    "p244": {
      "source_hash": "d3f62d5f7685",
      "text": "See a strange sunset? Think:"
    },
    "p245": {
      "source_hash": "5c2de61e8b3a",
      "text": "what's extra in the air today?"
    },
    "p246": {
      "source_hash": "2d2658267269",
      "text": "More air changes colors. What about almost none?"
    },
    "p247": {
      "source_hash": "a876a7f387c3",
      "text": "Remember the first question? On the Moon, by day, look up."
    },
    "p248": {
      "source_hash": "6f35edeb1a17",
      "text": "On the Moon..."
    },
    "p249": {
      "source_hash": "81814b978776",
      "text": "is there air?"
    },
    "p250": {
      "source_hash": "6be203fcda20",
      "text": "Almost none. Only a very, very thin trace."
    },
    "p251": {
      "source_hash": "ff7d85152b80",
      "text": "No air, no little balls"
    },
    "p252": {
      "source_hash": "83f42106a8dc",
      "text": "to bounce blue to me..."
    },
    "p253": {
      "source_hash": "9b0fab01141b",
      "text": "So the sky is black!"
    },
    "p254": {
      "source_hash": "8d10051d754a",
      "text": "Yes. The sun is bright, yet the Moon's daytime sky is black."
    },
    "p255": {
      "source_hash": "016312066e83",
      "text": "Bright ground under a pitch-black sky."
    },
    "p256": {
      "source_hash": "13692b95dc05",
      "text": "Oh!"
    },
    "p257": {
      "source_hash": "fe4f29613937",
      "text": "Remember my blue and red from the roof?"
    },
    "p258": {
      "source_hash": "85dfb2550853",
      "text": "Same light,"
    },
    "p259": {
      "source_hash": "4b7ec82c8b10",
      "text": "short path and long path!"
    },
    "p260": {
      "source_hash": "728f29b2d2b8",
      "text": "Next time you look up, think:"
    },
    "p261": {
      "source_hash": "28af7ff0a8ae",
      "text": "how far did this light travel to reach you?"
    },
    "p262": {
      "source_hash": "36d742bcb996",
      "text": "So that's why!"
    },
    "p263": {
      "source_hash": "bf70b61e7d63",
      "text": "Your best sunset color ever?"
    },
    "p264": {
      "source_hash": "0e4e1b6625fb",
      "text": "Where? Tell us in comments."
    },
    "p265": {
      "source_hash": "88de677d4daa",
      "text": "Want to find life's whys with us? Subscribe to So That's Why."
    }
  }
}
